% A measure phrase used as degree specifier of an adjective (two inches too
% short) introduces a two-place 'measure' relation between the adjective's
% eventuality and the measured instance.
%
% ERS fingerprint (https://delph-in.github.io/docs/erg/ErgSemantics_MeasurePhrases/):
%   h0:measure[ARG0 e1, ARG1 e2, ARG2 x]
%   h0:[ARG0 e2]
%   h1:[ARG0 x]

pattern { M [pred="measure"]; M -[1=ARG1]-> A; M -[1=ARG2]-> X }
